## Why This Is Asked
Tests mastery of amortized batching, range updates, and exact coverage checks on a line, common in streaming analytics and scheduling systems.

## Key Concepts
- Coordinate compression, segment tree with range updates, global min check, amortized batching, space efficiency.

## Code Example
```javascript
class SegTree {
  constructor(n){ this.n=n; this.min=Array(4*n).fill(0); this.cover=Array(4*n).fill(0); this.lazy=Array(4*n).fill(0); }
  _apply(i,delta){ this.cover[i]+=delta; this.min[i]+=delta; this.lazy[i]+=delta; }
  _push(i){ if(this.lazy[i]!==0){ this._apply(i*2,this.lazy[i]); this._apply(i*2+1,this.lazy[i]); this.lazy[i]=0; } }
  update(qL,qR,delta,i=1,l=0,r=this.n-1){ if(qR<l||r<qL) return; if(qL<=l&&r<=qR){ this._apply(i,delta); return; } this._push(i); const m=(l+r)>>1; this.update(qL,qR,delta,i*2,l,m); this.update(qL,qR,delta,i*2+1,m+1,r); this.min[i]=Math.min(this.min[i*2],this.min[i*2+1]); }
  fullCovered(){ return this.min[1]>0; }
}
``` 

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle intervals with dynamic endpoints or non-integer endpoints?
- How would you adapt to non-uniform batch sizes or streaming deletions without prior insertions?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical amortized analysis under streaming appends with cache considerations. It evaluates understanding of how to design data structures that balance update frequency, query latency, and memory access patterns.

## Key Concepts
- **Sliding windows**: Maintaining a fixed-size view over streaming data
- **Circular buffers**: O(1) rotation without shifting elements
- **Amortized analysis**: Batched updates spread costs over time
- **Cache-friendly layout**: Sequential memory access patterns for spatial locality

## Code Example
```javascript
class StreamingAnalyticsStore {
  constructor(W, kQueries, mKeys) {
    this.W = W;
    this.blocks = [];
    this.head = 0;
    this.size = 0;
    this.windowSum = 0;
    this.queryRanges = kQueries.map(([start, end]) => ({ start, end }));
    this.keySet = new Set(mKeys);
  }

  appendBatch(newBlocks) {
    for (const block of newBlocks) {
      if (this.size === this.W) {
        this.windowSum -= this.blocks[this.head];
      }
      this.blocks[this.head] = block;
      this.windowSum += block;
      this.head = (this.head + 1) % this.W;
      this.size = Math.min(this.size + 1, this.W);
    }
  }

  rangeSum(queryIndex) {
    const { start, end } = this.queryRanges[queryIndex];
    const windowSize = this.size;
    const startIdx = (this.head - end + this.W) % this.W;
    const endIdx = (this.head - start - 1 + this.W) % this.W;
    let sum = 0;
    let i = startIdx;
    while (i !== (endIdx + 1) % this.W) {
      sum += this.blocks[i];
      i = (i + 1) % this.W;
    }
    return sum;
  }

  hasKey(key) {
    return this.keySet.has(key);
  }
}
```

